en.use:
Use to assess the clinical or pathological stage group for melanoma based on the T, N, and M categories. 

The guideline maps the individual TNM components to the overall prognostic stage;

stage 0: Tis, N0, M0;

stage IA: T1a, N0, M0 OR T1b, N0, M0;

stage IB: T2a, N0, M0 OR T1b, N0, M0;

stage IIA: T2b, N0, M0 OR T3a, N0, M0;

stage IIB: T4a, N0, M0 OR T3b, N0, M0;

stage IIC: T4b, N0, M0;

stage III: Any T, N >= 1 , M0

stage IIIA: T1–2a, N1a, M0 OR T1–2a, N2a, M0;

stage IIIB: T0–2a, N1b–c, M0 OR T1–2a, N2b, M0 OR T2b–3a, N1a–2b or N1c, M0;

stage IIIC: T0, N2b–c or N3b–c, M0 OR T1a–3a, N2c or N3a–c, M0 OR T3b–4a, Any ≥ N1, M0 OR T4b, N1a–2c, M0;

stage IIID: T4b, N3a–c, M0;

stage IV: Any T, Any N, M1.
